Licensor: the author of PDF-Knead, owner of the GitHub account “systemswap”, hereinafter “Licensor”. If the account is renamed, this
means its owner under the current name.

The source code of PDF-Knead is available to read, but PDF-Knead is not open-source software. Almost everything in PDF-Knead is free
for everyone, for any purpose. Only eight features require a license for commercial use – and only after a free introductory period
until 31 December 2027; whoever starts later can try them free of charge for three months.


1 Definitions

(1) “Software”: the program PDF-Knead in executable form and as source code together with the files of its project, without the
    components of other projects (section 9).
(2) “Results”: files and printouts created or edited with the Software.
(3) “Commercial use”: any use by or for companies, self-employed persons and freelancers in the course of their work, and by
    authorities and other public administration bodies – including use by their employees or agents. Use by associations that are
    not non-profit and have full-time employees paid by the association is also commercial.
(4) “Non-commercial use”:
    a) use by private individuals for private purposes,
    b) use by educational institutions – schools, universities, adult education centres and other public or state-recognized
       educational institutions – for teaching, training and research,
    c) use by non-profit organizations (for example animal shelters),
    d) use by associations without full-time employees paid by the association.
(5) “Licensed features”: redaction; measuring; signing with a certificate (digital signature); converting to PDF/A and saving as
    PDF/A; scanning; creating forms (adding and designing form fields, recognizing fields); editing the page content (changing text,
    pictures, codes and fields of the page); removing restrictions (lifting the permissions and passwords of a file). The Software
    marks them.
(6) “Free features”: all other features – in particular viewing, searching, printing, filling in forms, the handwritten signature,
    verifying digital signatures, opening and checking PDF/A files, and creating and checking e-invoices.
(7) “Introductory period”: the period up to and including 31 December 2027, extended where applicable under section 3 (5).
    “Trial”: three months from the day the Software is first used commercially on a computer. “Free period”: the introductory
    period or, if it ends later, the trial.
(8) “Commercial distribution”: any distribution or provision of the Software that earns money – in particular against payment, as
    part of a paid product or offer, through download offers financed by fees or advertising, or as a service for others (for
    example over the internet) for which payment is charged. Training courses under section 5 (3) are not commercial distribution.
(9) “License key”: the key the Licensor issues with a commercial license. Among other things it names the licensee, the unlocked
    features and the end of the update period.


2 Use without a license fee

(1) For non-commercial use, the Software may be used with all features without a license fee and without a time limit.
(2) For commercial use, the free features may be used without a license fee and without a time limit.
(3) For commercial use, the licensed features may also be used without a license fee during the free period.


3 Licensed features in commercial use

(1) After the end of the free period, commercial use of the licensed features requires a commercial license, granted by the
    Licensor in a separate contract. Scope, update period and price follow from that contract.
(2) A commercial license applies without a time limit to all versions of the Software released up to the end of its update period.
    It applies to versions released later only if the update period has been extended. Before an update, the Software points out
    when a new version is no longer covered by the license.
(3) At first start, the Software asks for the kind of use. The answer is a self-declaration; it must be correct and must be updated
    when the kind of use changes. It stays on the computer and is not transmitted.
(4) After the end of the free period, the Software locks the licensed features in commercial use until a matching license
    key is entered. Opening, viewing and saving always remain possible, including for files edited with licensed features. The lock
    is an aid to complying with the license, not copy protection; this license is authoritative.
(5) The Licensor may extend the introductory period or release licensed features permanently, by announcement on the project page
    or through the Software. Shortening it is excluded.
(6) A license key may only be used by the licensee and within the agreed scope, and must not be passed on to third parties.
(7) License inquiries go to the Licensor through the project page on GitHub (https://github.com/systemswap/PDF-Knead).
(8) Voluntary support (for example through Ko-fi) is welcome but does not replace a commercial license.


4 Results

The Results belong to the user. This license does not restrict their use; they may also be sold. Rights of third parties in the
processed content remain unaffected.


5 Distribution of the Software

(1) The unmodified Software may be distributed as long as no money is earned with it. It must be distributed complete, together
    with this license, the file THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md and the license texts of the components of other projects.
(2) Any commercial distribution is not permitted; in particular, the Software must not be sold as one's own program. The Licensor
    reserves the distribution of the Software.
(3) Training courses on the Software may be offered, also against payment. Participants receive the Software free of charge or
    download it themselves; no payment may be charged for the Software itself. The trainer's own use of the Software is subject to
    sections 2 and 3.


6 Modifications

(1) The Software may be modified for one's own use. The obligations under section 3 also apply to modified versions.
(2) Modified versions may be distributed if
    a) no money is earned with them,
    b) the complete source code of the modified version is supplied or made available free of charge,
    c) the changes are marked with their date,
    d) the modified version is distributed under this license in the same version, and
    e) it carries the notice “based on PDF-Knead” with a reference to the project page and does not use the name under section 8
       as its own product name.
(3) In distributed versions, the question about the kind of use, the marking and locking of the licensed features, the check of the
    license key, and license and copyright notices must not be removed, altered or circumvented.


7 Use of parts of the code

(1) Individual parts of the source code may be used in one's own non-commercial projects. Using the Software as a whole or
    substantial parts of it is not permitted; section 6 applies to that.
(2) Such projects may be published as long as no money is earned with them.
(3) Every such use must name PDF-Knead as the source, with a reference to this license. The parts taken over remain under this
    license.


8 Name

The name “PDF-Knead” must not be used for other products, for modified versions or for parts taken over, nor in a way that suggests
the Licensor is behind another offer. Mentioning it factually, for example as the source under section 6 (2) e) and section 7,
remains permitted.


9 Components of other projects

The Software contains components of other projects. Only their own licenses apply to them; they are listed in the file
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md, and their license texts accompany the Software. This license does not restrict the rights in these
components.


10 Contributions

The Licensor currently does not accept contributions to the code. Bug reports and suggestions are welcome; they do not create any
rights in the Software.


11 Violations

(1) Anyone who violates this license loses the rights under it.
(2) If a violation is remedied within 30 days after the Licensor has pointed it out, the rights continue. This applies to the first
    violation; further claims of the Licensor remain unaffected.


12 Liability and warranty

(1) Under this license, the Software is provided free of charge and without warranty, as it is.
(2) The Licensor is liable only for intent and gross negligence, for injury to life, body or health, and under the German Product
    Liability Act. Otherwise, liability is excluded, in particular for loss of data, lost profit and consequential damage.
(3) The user backs up his files before editing them and checks the Results before passing them on or using them. In particular:
    - Redaction and cleanup: the user checks whether confidential content has actually been removed before passing on a file. It
      is not promised that every kind of hidden content is detected.
    - Digital signatures: they are not qualified electronic signatures. No promise is made about their legal effect in a given case.
    - Measuring: measured values depend on the scale and accuracy of the document; the user checks them before using them.
    - Converting to PDF/A: the Software checks the result against the rules shown. It is not promised that every body requiring
      PDF/A accepts the result.
    - Compression, conversion and scanning: quality may be lost; keep the original.
    - E-invoice check: the check is an aid. It makes no statement about the tax or legal validity of an invoice; its rules reflect
      the state shown. The user checks the invoice himself.
(4) For holders of a commercial license, liability and warranty follow their contract.


13 Later versions

(1) New versions of the Software may be released under a changed license. A version already received remains under the license
    with which it was received.
(2) For versions received under version 1.0 of this license, this version may be applied instead.


14 Final provisions

(1) The law of the Federal Republic of Germany applies, excluding the UN Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods.
(2) If the licensee is a merchant, a legal entity under public law or a special fund under public law, the place of jurisdiction is
    the Licensor's seat.
(3) If a provision of this license is invalid, the others remain valid.
(4) The German version is authoritative. The English version is a translation for information.


